BT /F2 13 Tf 72 595 Td (1. Purpose and Scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 575 Td (This policy establishes the framework for regulating access to data used by artificial) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 562 Td (intelligence systems within MT&T Corporation. It applies to all employees, contractors,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 549 Td (partners, and automated systems that access, process, or generate data through AI/ML) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 536 Td (platforms deployed on the Databricks Lakehouse Platform.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 513 Td (The policy covers all workspaces, model serving endpoints, AI Gateway configurations,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 500 Td (foundation model APIs, vector search indexes, and Genie rooms operating within MT&T's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 487 Td (Databricks environment.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 72 454 Td (2. Data Classification for AI Systems) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 434 Td (All data accessed by AI systems must be classified into one of four tiers: \(a\) Public - Data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 421 Td (that can be freely used for AI training and inference, \(b\) Internal - Data restricted to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 408 Td (internal AI applications with standard access controls, \(c\) Confidential - Data requiring) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 395 Td (enhanced controls including audit logging, encryption at rest and in transit, and role-based) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 382 Td (access, \(d\) Restricted - Data that requires explicit approval from the Data Governance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 369 Td (Council before AI processing, including PII, PHI, financial records, and customer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 356 Td (communications.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 333 Td (AI models trained on Confidential or Restricted data must be tagged in Unity Catalog with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 320 Td (appropriate sensitivity labels. Model serving endpoints exposing such models must implement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 307 Td (AI Gateway guardrails to prevent data leakage in responses.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 72 274 Td (3. Access Control Requirements) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 254 Td (All AI platform access must use Unity Catalog-managed identities. Service principals must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 241 Td (used for automated workflows and model serving endpoints. Personal access tokens are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 228 Td (prohibited for production AI workloads.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 205 Td (Access to model serving endpoints must follow the principle of least privilege. Each endpoint) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 192 Td (must have an explicit access control list \(ACL\) defining which users, groups, and service) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 179 Td (principals can invoke it. Wildcard permissions \(ALL USERS\) are prohibited for endpoints) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 166 Td (serving Confidential or Restricted data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 143 Td (Cross-workspace access to AI resources requires approval from both the source and destination) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 130 Td (workspace administrators. All cross-workspace AI data flows must be documented in the AI Data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 117 Td (Flow Registry maintained in the cmegdemos_catalog.ai_governance schema.) Tj ET
